quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,142,The foolish among the people will say (about the Muslims): ‘What has turned them away from the direction of prayer they were following before?’ Say: ‘The East and the West belong to Allah. He guides whomever He likes to the straight path.’
  2,143,"Thus (O Muslims!) We have made you a just and moderate nation so that you may be witnesses for humankind and that the Messenger (Muhammad [blessings and peace be upon him]) may be a witness for you. Moreover, We appointed your former prayer direction (the Qibla) only to distinguish those who faithfully follow the Messenger from those who turn back on their heels. So, this (change of prayer direction) was a difficult test, except for those whom Allah had guided. However, Allah would not let your faith be in vain. Indeed, Allah is Most Kind (and) All-Merciful to humankind."
  2,144,"(O Beloved Prophet!) Indeed, We have seen you turning your face towards heaven (during your prayer). So, We will surely turn you towards a prayer direction that pleases you. So turn your face towards the direction of the Sacred Mosque; wherever you (believers) may be, turn your faces towards it. Those given the Book surely know this is the truth from their Lord. And Allah is not negligent of what they do."
  2,145,"So even if you bring every proof to those given the Book, they would not follow your prayer direction, nor would you follow their prayer direction; nor would any of their sects follow the prayer direction of others. And if you yield to their desires, after the knowledge that has come to you, you will indeed be one of the wrongdoers."
